      "side": 1,
      "message": "You declare in the Gwendolin dts file:\n```\n\t\t/* First 128 kB (uniform 4 kB sectors) used for RO */\n\t\twp-ro {\n\t\t\toffset \u003d \u003c0x0\u003e;\n\t\t\tsize \u003d \u003c0x20000\u003e;\n\t\t\tec-ro {\n\t\t\t\tpad-byte \u003d \u003c0xff\u003e;\n\t\t\t};\n\t\t};\n```\n`key-ro` is a public key for RWSIG and it is placed at the end of RO so 0x20000 - 0x400(key size) \u003d 0x1fc00. I don\u0027t know why it is `0x1ec40`. @davidmcross@google.com can you share some explanation?",
      "parentUuid": "82590113_de33c8e8",
